    <item>
      <title>My learnings from &#34;A guide to convolution arithmetic for deep learning&#34;</title>
      <link>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/deep_learning_paper_reading_1/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 11 Aug 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/deep_learning_paper_reading_1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Vincent Dumoulin and Francesco Visin. &amp;ldquo;A Guide to Convolution Arithmetic for Deep Learning.&amp;rdquo; arXiv preprint arXiv:1603.07285, 2016. &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.07285&#34;&gt;https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.07285&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-9.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-3.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-5.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-4.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-6.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-8.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-10.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-11.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-15.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-19.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-22.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-20.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-21.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;agtcafdl-23.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>From, Into traits</title>
      <link>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/from_into/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 07 Sep 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/from_into/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s say we have a user-defined type &lt;code&gt;Point&lt;/code&gt; defined as follows&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-rust&#34; data-lang=&#34;rust&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Point&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    x: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;i32&lt;/span&gt;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    y: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;i32&lt;/span&gt;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;and we want a &lt;code&gt;String&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;str&lt;/code&gt; of the form &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;(1,2)&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt; to be converted into &lt;code&gt;Point&lt;/code&gt; type. We need to implement&#xA;the &lt;code&gt;From&lt;/code&gt; trait on the &lt;code&gt;Point&lt;/code&gt; type so that we can do something like&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-rust&#34; data-lang=&#34;rust&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; p: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Point&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Point::from(String::from(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;(1,2)&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;));&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;or&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-rust&#34; data-lang=&#34;rust&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; p: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Point&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Point::from(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;(1,2)&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The rust std library documentation says only to implement &lt;code&gt;From&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;since &lt;code&gt;From&amp;lt;T&amp;gt; for U implies Into&amp;lt;U&amp;gt; for T&lt;/code&gt; which means by implementing the &lt;code&gt;From&lt;/code&gt; trait on&#xA;the &lt;code&gt;Point&lt;/code&gt; type, we can make use of the standard library implementation of the &lt;code&gt;Into&lt;/code&gt; trait. We can now also do&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Iterators on user-defined types, Part-1</title>
      <link>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/iterators-1/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 03 Sep 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/iterators-1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s say we have a user-defined type &lt;code&gt;Dictionary&lt;/code&gt; which is defined as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-rust&#34; data-lang=&#34;rust&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Dictionary&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    words: Vec&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;String&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;impl&lt;/span&gt; Dictionary {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt;() -&amp;gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Self&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        Dictionary { words: Vec::new() }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;insert&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;mut&lt;/span&gt; self, val: String) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        self.words.push(val);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We would like to implement an iterator on our &lt;code&gt;Dictionary&lt;/code&gt; type so that we can loop over all the words in the dictionary like&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-rust&#34; data-lang=&#34;rust&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;mut&lt;/span&gt; dict &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Dictionary::new();&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dict.insert(String::from(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;abashed&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;));&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dict.insert(String::from(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;abashings&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;));&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dict.insert(String::from(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;abashment&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;));&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;dict.insert(String::from(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;abate&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;));&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; word &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; dict {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;println!&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, word);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rust provides us with the &lt;code&gt;Iterator&lt;/code&gt; trait which can be used to implement iterator on user-defined types. But the loop in the above code snippet, actually converts the &lt;code&gt;dict&lt;/code&gt; into an iterator. The two for loops in the code snippet below are equivalent&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Operator overloading in Rust</title>
      <link>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/operator_overloading/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 01 Sep 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/operator_overloading/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s say we have a user-defined type &lt;code&gt;Rational&lt;/code&gt; defined as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-rust&#34; data-lang=&#34;rust&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;#[derive(Debug)]&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Rational&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    num: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;i32&lt;/span&gt;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    den: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;i32&lt;/span&gt;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;In order to support arithmetic operators  like (&lt;code&gt;+&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;-&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;*&lt;/code&gt;) on &lt;code&gt;Rational&lt;/code&gt;, we would have to implement the &lt;code&gt;Add&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Sub&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Div&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Mul&lt;/code&gt; traits on &lt;code&gt;Rational&lt;/code&gt; from the Rust standard library. To implement the &lt;code&gt;Add&lt;/code&gt; trait&#xA;on &lt;code&gt;Rational&lt;/code&gt;, we need to provide an implementation for the &lt;code&gt;add&lt;/code&gt; method  from the &lt;code&gt;Add&lt;/code&gt; trait.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>How to compare user defined types in Rust</title>
      <link>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/comparing_user_defined_types/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 25 Aug 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/comparing_user_defined_types/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s just say we have a user-defined type Person defined as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-rust&#34; data-lang=&#34;rust&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Person&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;      name: String,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;      age: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;i32&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We need to compare two Persons &lt;code&gt;mat&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;mac&lt;/code&gt; defined as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-rust&#34; data-lang=&#34;rust&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; mat: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Person&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Person{name: String::from(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Mat&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;), age: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;30&lt;/span&gt;};&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; mac: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Person&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Person{name: String::from(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Mac&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;), age: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;35&lt;/span&gt;};&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We cannot just do &lt;code&gt;mat == mac&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;mat != mac&lt;/code&gt;. We have to define what equality means&#xA;for the type Person. We can do this in two ways.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Writing Man Pages</title>
      <link>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/man_pages/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chaitanyav.github.io/posts/man_pages/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I am writing about my experience working with man pages today.&#xA;I have never written/updated any man pages in the past. The&#xA;man page i updated was &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.freebsd.org/cgi/man.cgi?query=intro&amp;amp;sektion=3&amp;amp;manpath=FreeBSD+12.1-RELEASE+and+Ports&#34;&gt;intro(3)&lt;/a&gt; of&#xA;the FreeBSD Library Functions Manual.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Updating the man page involved going through the FreeBSD source code &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd/tree/master/lib&#34;&gt;src/lib&lt;/a&gt;  and figuring out the libraries that exist.&#xA;I came across many libraries which i had never heard of e.g. Performance Counters Library &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.freebsd.org/cgi/man.cgi?query=pmc&amp;amp;sektion=3&amp;amp;manpath=FreeBSD+12.1-RELEASE+and+Ports&#34;&gt;pmc(3)&lt;/a&gt; &amp;#x1f632;.And i had to find out which of those libraries have a man page so that they can be listed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
  </channel>
